From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: hevc: test switch for the packed
 10-bit output mode

On the J604 a 4K HEVC frame takes 0.42 ms longer to decode at 10 bits
than at 8, with the CPU idle, while macOS on the same SoC decodes both
at the same rate, also into a 16-bit-per-sample picture of the same size
and stride. The decoder has a packed 10-bit output mode, three samples
in 32 bits, which this driver never uses.

Add hevc_out_packed, a test-only parameter (default off) that decodes
10-bit HEVC pictures in that mode, so that the decoder can be timed in
both modes on the same stream. The CAPTURE format is not changed, so
the pictures are not usable while it is set.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
index 14954a3209..29b2e72553 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
@@ -31,6 +31,18 @@ module_param(hevc_frame_parse, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(hevc_frame_parse,
 		 "Read HEVC slice headers from Annex-B pictures sent without slice parameters (default: on)");
 
+/*
+ * Test switch (default off): write 10-bit HEVC pictures in the AVD's packed
+ * output mode (three 10-bit samples in 32 bits, macOS's default 'p420'
+ * layout) instead of 16-bit samples. The CAPTURE format stays P010, so the
+ * picture is not usable by a client; it exists to time the decoder in that
+ * mode against the default on the same stream.
+ */
+static bool hevc_out_packed;
+module_param(hevc_out_packed, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(hevc_out_packed,
+		 "Test only: decode 10-bit HEVC into the packed output mode (picture not usable); default off");
+
 bool avd_hevc_frame_parse_enabled(void)
 {
 	return READ_ONCE(hevc_frame_parse);
@@ -335,6 +347,8 @@ static void set_header(struct avd_ctx *ctx, struct avd_hevc_run *run)
 	bool is_intra = run->sl[0].slice_type == V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_TYPE_I;
 
 	push(AVD_OP_HDR | AVD_OP_HDR_FLAG_DECOMP(ctx->decomp) |
+		     AVD_OP_HDR_FLAG_PACKED(READ_ONCE(hevc_out_packed) &&
+					    sps->bit_depth_luma_minus8 == 2) |
 		     AVD_OP_HDR_FLAG_INTRA(is_intra) | AVD_OP_HDR_CONST |
 		     AVD_OP_HDR_FLAG_PIPE_STATE(
 			     !(avd->variant->quirks & AVD_QUIRK_NO_PIPE_STATE)),
-- 
2.43.0

